        "title": "Pass native agent option values through without allowlisting",
        "body": "Treat provider-native option values as pass-through configuration.\n\nGitWeave should validate only what it needs for its own graph contract, such as:\n\n- the option is present only on the relevant provider/node type\n- the value is a string when the native CLI expects a string\n\nDo not maintain hard-coded allowlists of native CLI option values unless a concrete GitWeave correctness requirement requires one.\n\nPass explicit values through unchanged and let the underlying Codex or Claude CLI accept or reject them.\n\nConceptually:\n\n```text\nGraph native option\n  \u2193\nGitWeave passes value through\n  \u2193\nCodex / Claude validates it\n```\n\nThis change implements the behavior above with focused regression coverage and documentation.\n\nValidation: deterministic regression tests and independent GitWeave review; GitHub CI on the published changes.\n\nCloses #40."
